WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.340
- So, Margo, can you explain
the story of the movie?

00:00:02.340 --> 00:00:06.480
- Well, Barbie Land is perfect,

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:10.590
and the Barbies are having
perfect day after perfect day.

00:00:10.590 --> 00:00:12.750
And everything's just
wonderful in Barbie Land,

00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:14.910
unless you're a Ken,

00:00:14.910 --> 00:00:17.400
or until you have an existential crisis,

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:19.020
which my Barbie does.

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:20.370
- What about the rest of you?

00:00:20.370 --> 00:00:21.270
Who's your Barbie?

00:00:21.270 --> 00:00:22.103
America, you can say.

00:00:22.103 --> 00:00:22.943
- I'm not a Barbie.

00:00:22.943 --> 00:00:25.500
I mean, I am a Barbie
'cause we're all Barbies.

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:27.660
Unless you're a Ken,
then you're not a Barbie.

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:30.963
But I'm a human in the movie.

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:33.270
- Because there's Barbie Land.

00:00:33.270 --> 00:00:34.590
- There's Barbie Land.

00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:36.480
And in the last trailer

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:39.240
you kind of see the hint of Barbie and Ken

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:41.220
are headed toward the real world.

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:44.013
And in the real world
my character, Gloria,

00:00:45.150 --> 00:00:49.620
encounters Barbie, and it's a connection.

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:52.200
And hijinks ensue from there.

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:54.271
And I think that's all I'm allowed to say.

00:00:54.271 --> 00:00:55.104
(all laughing)

00:00:55.104 --> 00:00:56.580
- And then, "I don't
wanna spoil everything."

00:00:56.580 --> 00:00:57.413
Who's your Barbie?

00:00:57.413 --> 00:00:58.246
Who do you play?

00:00:58.246 --> 00:00:59.670
- Did you guys ever have a Barbie,

00:00:59.670 --> 00:01:04.252
like the one Barbie that
you designate as like, her,

00:01:04.252 --> 00:01:06.450
(audience laughing)
where you cut their hair,

00:01:06.450 --> 00:01:07.650
burn their clothes,
- [Kelly] Test everything out.

00:01:07.650 --> 00:01:08.940
- And draw on them?

00:01:08.940 --> 00:01:10.143
That's the one I play.

00:01:13.367 --> 00:01:14.200
Mine were all them.
- Because, let's face it,

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:15.780
we all had one.

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:16.613
- Oh yeah.

00:01:16.613 --> 00:01:18.150
- You're like, "What
if I colored her hair?

00:01:18.150 --> 00:01:20.520
She needs a haircut."
(all laughing)

00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:21.420
I love your Barbie.

00:01:21.420 --> 00:01:23.130
Can you do the splits in real life,

00:01:23.130 --> 00:01:24.240
or did they have to like-

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:26.564
- I can go to about there,

00:01:26.564 --> 00:01:27.798
(all laughing)

00:01:27.798 --> 00:01:30.120
and then the whole system breaks down.

00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:30.953
I can't do a split.

00:01:30.953 --> 00:01:31.950
- Oh my God, way to go!

00:01:31.950 --> 00:01:33.900
Then the editing job is incredible.

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:35.970
- Oh no, they did this
whole technical thing

00:01:35.970 --> 00:01:39.933
where my legs are always at a 180.

